source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: Jira keeps reading the cell past the forced newline and renders both markers as items of one list inside it. jiro reads the row across both lines and keeps the whole table as raw Jira Markup, which is what preserves the list a GFM cell could not hold.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|* a\\
* b|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'><ul>
	<li>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" /></li>
	<li>b</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h||
|* a\\
* b|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
